{"id":37495634531121,"type":"album","name":"This Is Hardcore","artist":"Pulp","year":1998,"weight":28,"info":{"cover":"https://dn711204.ca.archive.org/0/items/mbid-83e396ab-d4b2-4220-96a2-54eb167ba63d/mbid-83e396ab-d4b2-4220-96a2-54eb167ba63d-17812149459.png","kind":"Single","tracks":2,"country":"GB","aoty":78,"aoty_user":82,"yt":"BQtmeyFQKN8","links":{"rateyourmusic":"https://rateyourmusic.com/release/album/pulp/this-is-hardcore","aoty":"https://www.albumoftheyear.org/album/3601-pulp-this-is-hardcore.php"},"desc":"The sixth album by English band Pulp, released 30 March 1998. It reached No. 1 in the UK Albums Chart, and was well received critically. The album was included in the book 1001 Albums You Must Hear Before You Die. In 2017, Pitchfork listed the album at number seven in its list \"The 50 Best Britpop Albums.\" ."},"artist_ref":{"id":115232158919769,"name":"Pulp","info":{"img":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Pulp_2012_cropped.jpg?width=500"}},"labels":[],"genres":[{"id":210192360016800,"type":"genre","name":"Alternative Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":2664,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":8412226417108,"type":"genre","name":"Indie Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":1139,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":238796249276494,"type":"genre","name":"Britpop","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":831,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":191826593279813,"type":"genre","name":"Art Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":531,"yt":null,"src":"musthear,rym"},{"id":68128513346957,"type":"genre","name":"Glam Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":463,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":236061900877969,"type":"genre","name":"Chamber Pop","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":245,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"}],"lists":[{"id":238350566072075,"name":"Pitchfork: The 50 Best Britpop Albums","src":"musthear","grp":"musicbrainz","list_year":null,"rank":7,"year":null,"note":null,"total":50,"scaruffi":null},{"id":118267099057662,"name":"AOTY Must Hear 1990s","src":"musthear","grp":null,"list_year":null,"rank":86,"year":null,"note":null,"total":432,"scaruffi":null},{"id":208356503087556,"name":"RYM Top — Rock — Art Rock","src":"musthear","grp":"rateyourmusic","list_year":null,"rank":86,"year":null,"note":null,"total":200,"scaruffi":null},{"id":199353246998089,"name":"Sputnikmusic Best Albums 1998","src":"charts","grp":"sputnikmusic","list_year":null,"rank":115,"year":1998,"note":null,"total":200,"scaruffi":null},{"id":192934750972716,"name":"1001 Albums You Must Hear Before You Die","src":"charts","grp":"1001 Albums","list_year":null,"rank":867,"year":1998,"note":null,"total":999,"scaruffi":null}],"podcast":[{"kind":"podcast","title":null,"body":"Released shortly after Pulp's departure from Britpop, this album was largely produced by Scott Walker (referred to as \"el biscocker\" in the transcript) and signaled a completely independent musical direction for the band. \"justo poco después acaba el disco hardcore ya prácticamente producido por ya el biscocker y seguía un camino completamente independiente.\"","year":1998,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Music Radar Clan","episode":"El BRIT POP como negocio discográfico","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=uIx0P0TssZ0"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":null,"body":"This album marked a significant departure from the Brit-Pop sound for Pulp, as Jarvis Cocker embraced a \"modern experimental\" approach, influenced by artists like Scott Walker. It is personally regarded by the speaker as the best album of Pulp's career, featuring passionate songs and moments where Jarvis Cocker's vocals evoke a James Bond-esque style. \"Jarvis Cocker passes completely the Brit-Pop and already gets into almost a modern experimental singer full of charisma that have passionate songs within this album.\"","year":1998,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Music Radar Clan","episode":"PULP: Pilares del Brit Pop","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0r8_s6hR3Ss"}]}],"book_tracks":[],"others":[{"id":1782162